Find the smallest positive value of \(a\) such that the equation \[
\sqrt{x^2 + (y - a)^2} = \sqrt{2} \cdot \sqrt{x^2 + (y + a)^2}
\] has exactly one real and nonnegative solution for \(y\) when \(x = 0\). Express your answer as a common fraction.

Find the number of solutions to the equation \( k^2 - 3k + 2 = 0 \) and identify which values of \( k \) ensure the columns of the matrix \[
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & k \\
2 & 4 \\
\end{bmatrix}
\] are linearly independent.

Find the smallest positive integer \( n \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
n \equiv 1 \pmod{3} \\
n \equiv 2 \pmod{5} \\
n \equiv 3 \pmod{7}
\end{cases}
\]

Find the smallest positive integer \(x\) that satisfies:
1. \(x \equiv d \pmod{5}\);
2. \(x + d^2 \equiv 5 \pmod{6}\);
3. The product of the digits of \(x\) is divisible by \(d\).

Compute the sum of all such \(x\) in the range \(500 \le x < 800\).

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences and also ensures that \( x + 3 \) is a perfect square:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 3 \pmod{4} \\
x \equiv 5 \pmod{6} \\
x \equiv 7 \pmod{8}
\end{cases}
\]

The integer matrix \[
\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} r & 2 & 3 \\ 5 & t & u \\ v & 2 & w \end{pmatrix}
\] has the property that \(\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 5 \\ 19 \end{pmatrix}.\) Determine the values of \(r\), \(t\), \(u\), \(v\), and \(w\) that satisfy this property.

Find all real solutions to the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
x + y &= 5, \\
x^2 + y^2 &= 13.
\end{align*}

Find all positive integers \(x\) that satisfy the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 4 \pmod{7} \\
x \equiv 11 \cdot n - 1 \pmod{11}
\end{cases}
\]
where \(n\) is a non-negative integer.

Find all integer solutions (m, n) to the system
\[
\begin{cases}
\modval{m^2 + n^2}{5} = 2 \\
\modval{mn}{7} = 3
\end{cases}
